## Frequently Asked Questions

### Q: Can I lock apps on Android without installing an app?
A: Yes, on most phones. Use Secure Folder on Samsung, Private space on Android 15 or later, or App lock on Xiaomi. App pinning works on any Android phone for the moment you hand it to someone.

### Q: Does Samsung have an app lock?
A: Not one that locks an app where it is. Samsung's answer is Secure Folder, which holds a locked copy of the app. Find it under `Settings > Security and privacy > More security settings`.

### Q: How do I lock WhatsApp on Android?
A: In WhatsApp, go to `Settings > Privacy > App lock` and turn it on. On Samsung you can also add WhatsApp to Secure Folder, and on Android 15 or later to Private space.

### Q: Does locking an app hide its notifications?
A: With Private space, yes: apps in a locked Private space are stopped and show no notifications. For other methods it depends on the phone, so check your lock screen notification settings too.

### Q: Can someone who knows my PIN open my locked apps?
A: If the lock uses your screen lock, yes. Give Secure Folder or Private space its own passcode, different from the one on your lock screen.

### Q: Can I see who tried to open my locked apps?
A: Android's and Samsung's app locks keep no record and take no photo. To see who tried to get into the phone itself, an app like CrookCatcher photographs anyone who enters a wrong PIN on the lock screen.

